{
  "info": {
    "name": "Ava API",
    "_postman_id": "8f3d1c42-6a51-4c7e-9a1b-0d2f5e7c9b10",
    "description": "Multi-tenant Go API \u2014 auth, tenants with roles, and the onboarding flow engine.\n\n## Getting started\n\n1. `docker compose up -d postgres` then `make dev` (or `make run`).\n2. Send **Auth \u203a Register**, then verify the email (see that request's description for how to read the token out of the database locally).\n3. Send **Auth \u203a Login** \u2014 the access and refresh tokens are captured into collection variables automatically, and every protected request inherits them.\n\n## How auth works here\n\nThe collection sends `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` by default; public endpoints override that to no-auth. A token is scoped to **one tenant**: it carries the tenant id and the caller's role in it. To act in another tenant use **Switch tenant**, which revokes the current session and issues a new one.\n\n## Tokens that arrive by email\n\nEmail verification, password reset, and invitations all send a link. With no `RESEND_API_KEY` set, sending fails (logged as a warning) and the request still succeeds \u2014 read the token from Postgres, as each of those requests describes.\n\n## Rate limits\n\n100 requests/minute per IP globally, 25/minute on auth endpoints. A throttled auth call returns 429 `auth_rate_limited`.\n\n## Response envelope\n\nEvery response is `{ success, data, error: { code, message, details? } }`. Branch on `error.code`, not on the message text.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.test(\"envelope shape\", function () {",
          "    const body = pm.response.json();",
          "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('success');",
          "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('data');",
          "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('error');",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
